# Curve-fit LocationLink length

A valid `MorphologyGraph.CurveFitProcesses` run must not increase the sum of XY lengths of the LocationLinks involved (`MorphologyGraph.SumLocationLinkLengths`). Leave-one-out Catmull-Rom with window > 1 can pull a shaft node off the current polyline; `LimitOffsetToAvoidLengtheningLinks` refuses (or shrinks) that move.

- Do not remove the per-move gate or the `Debug.Assert` on process-chain hop sum.
- A single hop can still grow when another incident link shrinks more; the enforceable property is the unique-edge length sum, not one hop.
- New CurveFit / process-registration behavior: add or extend an **FsCheck** property in `AnnotationVizLibTests/FSCheck` (pin `Configuration.Replay`, use `QuickThrowOnFailure`). Do not pin the invariant to a single RC1 location ID.
- Prefer FsCheck (or another parameterized property) over one-off fixtures when the claim is an invariant over a family of graphs.
